<title>UK: NATWEST STARTS BUYING RANK SHRS IN BUY-BACK.</title>
<headline>NATWEST STARTS BUYING RANK SHRS IN BUY-BACK.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brokerage house NatWest started buying Rank Group Plc shares on behalf of the company, launching the group's 10 percent buy-back, dealers said.</p>
<p>The stock traded 4-1/2p higher at 344-1/2p by 1104 GMT with volume registering at 1.3 million shares.</p>
<p>NatWest, Rank's broker, declined to comment.  </p>
<p>Earlier on Friday, Rank confirmed it intended to start the buy-back of up to 83.6 million shares.</p>
<p>Rank's chief executive Andrew Teare told Reuters on Thursday the leisure company would buy back more of its own shares in the next few days than first envisaged.</p>
<p>-- Louise Ireland, London Newsroom +44 171 542 8712</p>
</text>
